 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 520296,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/f6fed6f693925e67.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Michael W Peck/ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>Botulism is a potentially fatal food-borne disease. It is caused by toxins from the bacteria <i>Clostridium botulinum</i> (<i>C. botulinum</i>). This bacteria produces spores, which are difficult to destroy. The graph shows the amount of time a sample needs to be heated based on temperature. Note the time scale is a log scale: Log 1 is 10 minutes, log 2 is 100 minutes and log 3 is 1,000 minutes.</p>\n<p>Which treatment would effectively kill the spores and be safe?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1016635,
     "content_html": "Heating for 120 minutes at 70 °C."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016636,
     "content_html": "Heating for 100 minutes at 75 °C."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016637,
     "content_html": "Heating for  300 minutes at 85°C."
    },
    {
     "id": 1016638,
     "content_html": "Heating for 30 minutes at 90°C."
    }
   ],
